  "necessity_paragraph": "The patient presents with recurrent episodes of palpitations and lightheadedness, raising concern for paroxysmal atrial fibrillation in the context of a personal history of transient ischemic attacks and cerebral infarction. To evaluate for potential arrhythmic causes of these transient cerebral ischemic events and guide anticoagulation management, a cardiac event monitoring study (CPT 93271) is ordered. This service is supported by the documented diagnosis codes Z86.73, G45.9, and I48.0, and directly addresses the transient cerebral ischemic events described in the clinical indication note."
